messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI tools become routine in offices and labs, and major jurisdictions implement broad AI regulation.",
      "detail": "Productivity rises unevenly as organizations learn to integrate AI with audits and safety requirements. Climate-related disasters intensify, pushing adaptation spending upward."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Global greenhouse gas emissions peak and plateau.",
      "detail": "Falling clean-energy costs and policy shifts offset growth in energy demand. Extreme weather remains severe due to accumulated warming."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Electric vehicles exceed 60% of new light-duty sales globally.",
      "detail": "Battery supply chains scale and charging networks mature. Oil demand growth stalls and begins a long decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Frontier AI can perform most professional tasks under supervision.",
      "detail": "Capabilities drive large gains in design, coding, and science, while misinformation and security risks require new safeguards and licensing."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "A fusion pilot plant produces sustained net electricity to the grid for limited periods.",
      "detail": "The milestone proves feasibility but leaves commercialization, reliability, and cost challenges for the 2040s."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Annual emissions fall roughly half from their peak; clean power dominates additions.",
      "detail": "Grid-scale storage, nuclear, and flexible demand stabilize high-renewables systems. Heat waves and droughts continue to test resilience."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "AI automates most knowledge work with human oversight; governance matures after several high-profile failures.",
      "detail": "Labor markets restructure with shorter workweeks and expanded income supports in many countries. Safety incidents without global catastrophe trigger tighter alignment standards."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global population peaks and stabilizes; warming reaches around 1.8–2.2°C above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Urbanization and education slow growth, while adaptation and health systems reduce climate mortality in wealthier regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Managed retreat and coastal protection reshape many shorelines.",
      "detail": "Insurance markets adapt to chronic risk, and major ports are rebuilt or relocated. Climate migration becomes a structured, ongoing policy domain."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Longevity therapies add a decade or more to average healthy lifespan in affluent regions.",
      "detail": "Age-related disease burdens fall, but access and pension reform remain contentious. Ethics around enhancement intensify."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Permanent lunar and Martian settlements operate with robust closed-loop life support.",
      "detail": "They rely on Earth for specialized components but achieve local production of essentials. Space industry standardizes in-situ resource use."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Planetary defense demonstrates a successful kinetic deflection of a small asteroid.",
      "detail": "Global coordination mechanisms for impact risk become institutionalized. Survey completeness for hazardous near-Earth objects improves markedly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Warming stabilizes near ~2.3–2.7°C with committed sea-level rise continuing past a meter.",
      "detail": "Some tipping elements are avoided; others partially activate, raising adaptation costs. Food systems rely on heat- and drought-resilient crops, protected agriculture, and trade."
    },
    {
      "year": 2125,
      "event": "A cislunar economy matures, including space-based solar power beaming energy to Earth and habitats.",
      "detail": "High-precision manufacturing and propellant depots reduce launch dependence. Space traffic management and debris mitigation are routine."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Emergency geoengineering is used sparingly under strict international oversight after a near-miss with abrupt warming.",
      "detail": "Short-lived stratospheric aerosol deployments buy time for adaptation and carbon removal. Global norms treat such measures as temporary, last-resort tools."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Brain–computer interfaces and genetic enhancement become mainstream, expanding definitions of personhood.",
      "detail": "Memory, sensory, and cognitive augmentation shift education and work. Law recognizes hybrid and synthetic minds with rights and responsibilities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Ecosystem engineering and carbon removal restore major corridors and some lost functions.",
      "detail": "Rewilding and assisted migration rebuild partial biodiversity, though many extinctions remain irreversible. Methane and nitrous oxide controls mature."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Sea level rises 2–3 meters relative to 2000; coastal megacities are relocated or heavily defended.",
      "detail": "Cultural heritage is moved inland or elevated. New urban forms emphasize modularity, cooling, and water security."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Multiple self-sufficient habitats exist throughout the inner Solar System.",
      "detail": "Nuclear, solar, and beamed power enable routine fast transfers. Governance experiments diversify across habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Cultural and linguistic landscapes are unrecognizable to 21st-century observers.",
      "detail": "Continuity is preserved through curated archives and AI translators spanning millennia. Values evolve as lifespans lengthen and environments diversify."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Earth’s climate is actively managed with long-horizon feedback control.",
      "detail": "Orbital, land, ocean, and atmospheric interventions keep key parameters within agreed bounds. Stewardship institutions focus on equity across generations."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Post-biological and hybrid intelligences make up a large share of sapient populations.",
      "detail": "Baseline humans persist by choice and culture. Energy abundance shifts bottlenecks to materials, computation, and heat dissipation."
    },
    {
      "year": 3300,
      "event": "Uncrewed, slow probes reach nearby stars and return data; no confirmed extraterrestrial civilizations are found.",
      "detail": "Interstellar exploration proceeds cautiously with high redundancy. The Fermi paradox remains unresolved."
    },
    {
      "year": 3600,
      "event": "Descendant lineages diverge culturally and biologically; 'human' becomes an umbrella term.",
      "detail": "Some lineages are no longer inter-fertile with baseline humans. Legal systems center personhood on cognition, welfare, and consent rather than species."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Civilization weathers several regional collapses and recoveries without global extinction.",
      "detail": "Resilience improves via distributed infrastructure, knowledge vaults, and off-world redundancy. Lessons from failures are institutionalized."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Some off-world societies become fully independent of Earth.",
      "detail": "Trade and cultural exchange continue despite multi-hour communication delays and divergent norms. Political pluralism across habitats is the norm."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Distributed solar collectors in space harvest a substantial fraction of solar output accessible to civilization.",
      "detail": "Energy constraints ease, but governance focuses on thermal emissions, orbital ecology, and equitable allocation."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Glacial cycles remain suppressed by deliberate climate management.",
      "detail": "Long-term records and automated guardians maintain continuity across institutional turnovers. Planetary engineering is routine but conservative."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Multiple descendant lineages are genetically distinct enough to be separate species by biological criteria.",
      "detail": "Interoperability persists through cultural bridges and technology when desired. Diversity of form and mind is celebrated and contested."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Self-healing archives and cultural 'seed vaults' are distributed across Earth and space habitats.",
      "detail": "Redundant knowledge systems mitigate loss from disasters and political upheaval. Education incorporates millennia-scale context."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Earth’s biosphere supports rich, adapted ecosystems despite permanent human influence.",
      "detail": "Some extinct lineages are reintroduced from preserved genomes where habitats allow. Novel ecosystems are managed for function and resilience."
    },
    {
      "year": 9500,
      "event": "Cumulative existential risk remains nonzero; some branches of civilization fade, others flourish.",
      "detail": "Redundancy and dispersion reduce the chance of total loss, but coordination failures and rare catastrophes still occur. Long-run survival is path-dependent."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Outcomes range from a plural, spacefaring civilization to fragmented regional remnants on Earth.",
      "detail": "Given millennia of uncertainty, both persistence and loss are plausible; expansion beyond Earth improves the odds of continuity but does not guarantee it."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity likely endures the turbulent 21st–22nd centuries by decarbonizing, adapting to climate change, and integrating increasingly powerful AI under maturing governance. Over millennia, expansion into space, diversification of minds and bodies, and long-horizon stewardship greatly improve resilience, yet cumulative existential risk keeps ultimate outcomes uncertain. By year 10000, descendants of humanity may persist in many forms across multiple habitats—or, less likely but possible, be reduced to remnants or lost."
}
